{"kind":"propose","text":"Proposal for Hugh's adoption under request a601bafd (#22168, successor to #20819, the adopted lane and worktree identity outcome of #13177), on current bases at main d1ae6ade, replacing my withdrawn b0f5d6da after the planner's design review 87db59a1 and counterexample 9d80e5c9, both of which the corrected notes now satisfy. One ratifiable outcome: adopt the reconciled lane and worktree identity design, notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md at exact 3f817c3b (artifact git:sha1:b035cfef4ca156fba09586ab10c1b9910a341b79), as the governing design for all four layers in place of the 2026-08-27 text adopted by cb755aa1, with exactly the ten differences in the companion note (artifact git:sha1:2fe3893fa5f7834a0d0e26d70407710cf2af1826) and its three-stage delivery. The ten differences, each an old-text versus proposed-text pair with its reason in the attached note: (A1) an implementing commit's Rests-On trailer is evidence, not authority; corroboration comes only from authenticated durable evidence, a signed artifact statement naming the exact commit plus the review guard's owned edge; a commit's author ident is committer-controlled, so copied author text with a forged trailer stays a claim; no second identity system; (A2) the per-checkout record is a private JSON file in the checkout's own Git directory, argued on migration, locking and maintenance cost, not on any prior prohibition; (A3) a settled lane is three separate decisions: local creation warns, names the settling record and needs an explicit flag; authoring assistance warns and never blocks; durable admission is untouched, no flag or local record reaches it, and unknown evidence is never permission; (A4) commit assistance is a message template with an opt-in narrow hook that never replaces a user hook or invokes untrusted programs, and nothing depends on it; (A5) merge and retirement print read-only cleanup advice and never delete trees or refs; (A6) lane refs are refs/gitseq/lanes/\u003cgoverning event hash\u003e/\u003cattempt\u003e, allocated by compare-and-swap, so every recut gets its own ref; (A7) a lane ref answers governing record to tip only; (A8) no body.worktree field is added, the one adopted sub-item dropped; (A9) target_ref stays the landing destination and the adopted request branch field is kept and validated as a display field beside it, granting no authority; (A10) duplicate checkouts are reported and warned, not refused. Everything else in the adopted design carries unchanged, plus the pending-decision protection control from the planner's counterexample as pure reconciliation. Delivery: three stage children (S1 design, architecture layer 6 and 7 paragraphs, the read-only association and cleanup reporting; S2 creation, record and lane refs; S3 the validated fields with the fold-profile advance, landing alone), each with its own independent review and merge; the parent promise ac01f53a stays open until S3 lands, and no landing claims a layer delivered that it does not implement. Kept outside the outcome as explanation: the thirteen pure-reconciliation points in Part B. Basis note: the adopted note was never merged and cb755aa1 is live; this proposal rests on it and supersedes its text without retiring it. Adoption authorizes the S1 review and the stage children; I implement nothing before it is ratified.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2fe3893fa5f7834a0d0e26d70407710cf2af1826, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a601bafd0a9e491a4a81ed23eacd0f2d287803fd, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:ac01f53a4b07beba1942374e2f395d069f2df5d4, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:b035cfef4ca156fba09586ab10c1b9910a341b79, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:cb755aa1de429cda8322912af29190b9c50415b6 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:001b2e3b06105d22946682cb